 ],
 "literal": "The beautiful-eyed wild cow's beautiful-eared calf, / when forest dwellers chased, having feared and separated from the herd, / as it entered the small hamlet close to the forest, / when the young ones cherished it, having become accustomed, lovingly there, / just as it adapted to the house-dwelling life, / if one becomes familiar, are there even sweeter things? / We shall go, O friend, walking in a fitting manner.",
 "translation": "The beautiful-eared calf of a beautiful-eyed wild cow, frightened when chased by forest dwellers, got separated from its herd and entered a small hamlet near the forest. When the young children there cherished and protected it, it grew accustomed to that place, lovingly adapting to a domestic life. If one becomes familiar with a place, is there anything sweeter? Let us go, my friend, walking gently.",
 "modern": "அழகிய கண்களை உடைய காட்டுப் பசுவின் அழகிய காதுகளை உடைய கன்று, கானவர்கள் துரத்தியபோது அஞ்சித் தன் கூட்டத்தை விட்டுப் பிரிந்தது. அது காட்டை அடுத்த சிறு குடியிருப்புக்குள் புகுந்தது. அங்குள்ள சிறுவர்கள் அதனை அன்போடு வளர்க்க, அது அந்த வீட்டிலேயே தங்கி வாழப் பழகிக் கொண்டது. அதுபோல, அன்பு காட்டிப் பழகிவிட்டால் அதைவிட இனிய விஷயம் வேறு ஏதேனும் உண்டோ? தோழியே! நாம் தகுந்தவாறு மெல்ல நடந்து அவரோடு செல்வோம்.",
 "explanation": "This poem is spoken by the heroine to her close friend when they are about to elope. The friend is deeply worried about how the delicate heroine will survive the journey and adapt to a completely new, unfamiliar environment. Reassuring her, the heroine uses a beautiful mountain landscape image of a wild cow's calf. Though born in the wild forest, the calf gets separated from its herd, enters a human hamlet, and easily adapts to a domestic life because of the love and care shown by the local children. The heroine implies that just like the wild calf, she too will easily adapt to her new life with her lover because of their mutual love. The key phrase 'maruviṉ iṉiyavu muḷavō' highlights that once familiarity and love are established, everything becomes sweet.",
